      "message": "\u003e I believe that using FcPatternAdd(type) will add the element with a strong binding.\n\nI think you\u0027re right, let\u0027s try to lock in the invariants some.\n\n1) we only call `remove_weak` for `FC_FAMILY`.  let\u0027s rename it to `remove_weak_familiy` and drop the object param\n\n2) add some asserts at the top of the function:\n\n\n```\n  SkDEBUGCODE(\n      // We assume the pattern is non-empty and it starts with a strong family binding.\n      FcValue value;\n      FcValueBinding binding;\n      SkASSERT(FcPatternGetWithBinding(pattern, FC_FAMILY, 0, \u0026value, \u0026binding) \u003d\u003d FcResultMatch);\n      SkASSERT(binding \u003d\u003d FcValueBindingStrong);\n    );\n``` \n\n3) then we should be able to start the loop at index 1",
